{"title":"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd3b8e5167cdf49b523a1d212b5346cb9cd8257b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--(0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2)))--(-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--cycle,black+linewidth(.75)); MP(&quot;A&quot;,(-1,0),SW);MP(&quot;B&quot;,(1,0),SE);MP(&quot;C&quot;,(1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2)),E);MP(&quot;D&quot;,(0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2))),N);MP(&quot;E&quot;,(-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2)),W); dot((-1,0));dot((1,0));dot((1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2)));dot((-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2)));dot((0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2)))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>The convex pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa5b388ce4175f797cbe78bae18ae5f8863b760d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{A}=\\angle{B}=120^\\circ,EA=AB=BC=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"312\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca8e3408290ad6c3c56285e4a64391df8d08a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=DE=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" />. What is the area of ABCDE?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06038d47d151effcc8b511f342ea81bb5b9aff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 10\\quad \\text{(B) } 7\\sqrt{3}\\quad \\text{(C) } 15\\quad \\text{(D) } 9\\sqrt{3}\\quad \\text{(E) } 12\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"364\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726d99c659f45619b4fc1fd495b9844a3f46d70c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--(0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2)))--(-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--cycle,black+linewidth(.75)); draw((1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--(-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2))); draw((-1,0)--(-1,sqrt(2))); draw((1,0)--(1,sqrt(2))); MP(&quot;F&quot;,(-1,sqrt(2)),N);MP(&quot;G&quot;,(1,sqrt(2)),N); MP(&quot;A&quot;,(-1,0),SW);MP(&quot;B&quot;,(1,0),SE);MP(&quot;C&quot;,(1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2)),E);MP(&quot;D&quot;,(0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2))),N);MP(&quot;E&quot;,(-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2)),W); dot((-1,0));dot((1,0));dot((1+sqrt(2),sqrt(2)));dot((-1-sqrt(2),sqrt(2)));dot((0,sqrt(2)+sqrt(13-2*sqrt(2)))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>First, drop perpendiculars from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5980c5d4d98dc79330f1a12e592794203e81fd7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAB = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7503fd53505b51549b8390429ab5d3c841559782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAF = 30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951504e766abe296b6175ff16e530e8958f7753c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EAF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a 30-60-90 Triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2ef7f53ea2a97553977abe108af738f0516e67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae30b20846b1748b1c96e5a739893c3d9404ac7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = \\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c76c6d5a66a20aeaa65de229039bb065f05d5a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GB = \\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e14c849f0554b225a8b8738c159584c0ed019bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GC = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c9124875dc0a37a2d5e57049ba5b43c8d80ab757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FABG$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54e89719bed351e8e287e5ed52a8efe6086fa75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG = AB = 2$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Now, notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4afc1ff9023fa0428d6c48c184bfb574a183d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC = EF + FG + GC = 1+2+1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"312\" height=\"14\" />, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a9191aefcf2eb237d1999486083ed78f6d515f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is equilateral.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009ff7e205a05e4a85cd92fcd7c6f8eec87e52d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCDE] = [EABC]+[DCE] = \\frac{2+4}{2}(\\sqrt3)+\\frac{4^2\\cdot\\sqrt3}{4} = 3\\sqrt3+4\\sqrt3=\\boxed{7\\sqrt3 (B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"649\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>-AOPS81619\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME\" title=\"1993 AHSME\">1993 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1993 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 AHSME Pr